I also recommend the dagger and mithril tactics. And 16 int sucks for
wizards, as they will always hunger when casting spells. You need 20
Int.
I wouldn't use studded leather armor, it's super heavy and doesn't
provide much AC. Use dwarwish / elven mithril coats instead. Plus,
wear an orcish helm and boots; if you find some which are well-
enchanted, you might have an AC around -3 quite early. Combined with
an elven dagger and at least Basic skill in dagger, you'll be fine
without spellcasting.
For spellcasting, I recommend learning the Magic Missile spell early,
as you'll have a quite good chance to cast it even when wearing metal
armor. All the other spells can wait until you get SDSM (or, if it's
something like Identify, just take your armor off temporarily).

Second wish? Depends. I often wish for The Master Key of Thievery
(halved physical damage), as the earlier you wish for it, the lower
the chance another randomly-generated artifact will fool you. Other
good ideas include +2 blessed greased fixed speed boots, a blessed
amulet of life saving (never underestimate those, they may look like a
wasted wish, but they WILL save your ass, especially against
instadeaths. Neverthereless, Reflection has a higher priority.), or an
uncursed magic marker (always a good idea; then write a lot of enchant
armor scrolls; you might also wish for a blessed one if you are sure
you don't want to write cursed srolls).

